it is a story that we've all heard  sometimes too many times before a young  healthy person dying after contracting  covid19 and this time the virus took a  young mom in a matter of weeks now her  husband newborn daughter and the rest of  her family are left shocked and  devastated as they try to move forward  sasha loftus joining us now live tonight  to share their story  denise and brian kimmey was young  healthy and ready to welcome her first  child still covid19 came the virus stole  her away from those who loved her more  than anything  she was wonderful  loving generous and eternally joyful are  just a few words vera foster uses to  describe her sister kimmy just such a  happy loving  would take the shirt off her back for  anybody more than anything she and her  husband longed for a child of their own  and tried for years to live that dream  she finally got pregnant and that's all  she wanted she just wanted to be a mom  but before her baby girl was born covet  19 took hold of kimmy's world and after  weeks of fighting to breathe with oxygen  treatments and ventilators the 35 year  old died alone this week here at spring  valley hospital she never got to hold  her baby that she wanted so long it's  something vena wants no one else to go  through and she's asking for the same  support her family has felt since her  sister first got sick i'm just asking  for that same overwhelming love  to please be there now to help mike  her husband and this little baby  because they're going to need it this is  a lot for him and while kimmy may be  gone her warmth and light will live on  for generations to come i feel when that  day comes and i can hold that little  baby in my arms i'll be holding my  sister  now kami's family has started a gofundme  page to help her husband mike and her  newborn daughter jordan move forward  without her and of course to help with  funeral expenses if you'd like to help  their family we have more information on  our website  8newsnow.com reporting live in the  newsroom tonight sasha loftis 8 news now
 

